  "id": "COMPOUND:26415 - PROTEIN:5474",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate and SCC-9, through a series of target interactions involving palmarumycin CP18. This compound is a known inhibitor of P2X purinoceptors, which are ligand-gated ion channels expressed on cell surfaces. The drug targets both P2X purinoceptor 1 and P2X purinoceptor 7, which are involved in cellular signaling pathways that regulate cell survival, proliferation, and apoptosis. These receptors are implicated in the progression of cancer, particularly in SCC-9, a model of squamous cell carcinoma. The evidence suggests that the drug may exert its anti-cancer effects by modulating these receptors, thereby influencing cellular processes that contribute to tumor growth and metastasis. The consistent involvement of palmarumycin CP18 as a mediator in the relationship between the compound and SCC-9 underscores the potential for this drug to be a therapeutic agent in the treatment of this cancer.",
